I am sitting at my desk in the office.
Deepa is sitting next to me.
We are checking the new user interface on the computer screen.
At the time of the first meeting, this project had seemed very difficult.
But now this is a very easy, ordinary job.
Deepa pointed a finger to a part of the screen.
"Maya, we need a little more space below this button," she said.
"The letters are too close to the border."
I looked closely at the design.
What she said is right.
I immediately made that change in the code.
After that, I saved the file and refreshed the screen.
"How is it now?"
I asked Deepa.
"Yes, now it looks right," she said smiling.
With that, we finished the work for that page.
"Shall we go drink tea?"
Deepa asked.
I was also feeling a little tired.
"Okay, let's go to the breakroom," I replied.
